==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|schilt|g=m|t=shield}} (genitive {{m|gmh||schiltes}} or {{m|gmh||schildes}}), from {{inh|de|goh|skilt}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*skeldu}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*skelduz|t=shield}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*(s)keyt-|t=shield, cover}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|schild}}, {{cog|en|shield}}, {{cog|da|skjold}}.

The ''-ld-'' is due to sporadic revoicing, reinforced by unshifted forms in [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] (cf. {{m|de|dulden}}, {{m|de|Geld}} etc.). The neuter gender spread southward from {{der|de|gml|schilt}}. It established itself in general Standard German for the derived sense “sign”, but not for the traditional sense “shield”. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃɪlt/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schild.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schild2.ogg}}
* {{homophones|de|schilt}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n,es:s,er:e|dim=chen,lein,ken[rare, also Ruhrpöttisch]}}

# [[sign]], [[plate]] {{gloss|flat surface bearing information}}
#: {{ux|de|Was steht dahinten auf dem '''Schild'''?|What does that '''sign''' say over there?}}
# {{lb|de|often|also|diminutive}} [[label]], [[tag]] {{gloss|piece of paper etc. on a product}}
#: {{syn|de|Etikett}}
#: {{ux|de|Du musst noch das '''Schild''' an deinem neuen Hemd abschneiden.|You still have to cut off the '''label''' from your new shirt.}}
# {{lb|de|nonstandard|or|informal|northern and central Germany}} {{alternative form of|de|Schild|t=shield, protector|pos=noun 2 below}}
#: {{ux|de|Mittelalterliche '''Schilde(r)''' waren oft sehr schwer.|Medieval '''shields''' were often quite heavy.}}
#: {{ux|de|Die Stasi begriff sich als (das) '''Schild''' und Schwert der Partei.|The [[Stasi]] considered itself the Party’s [i.e. the SED's] '''shield''' and sword.}}

====Usage notes====
* In official use, {{m|de||Schild}} in the sense of “shield, protector” is exclusively masculine. However, in northern and central Germany the word is also used in the neuter form (plural {{m|de||Schilder}}) with no difference made between the senses.<ref name="Wiener Zeitung">[http://www.wienerzeitung.at/meinungen/glossen/389738_Der-Schild-oder-das-Schild.html Der Schild oder das Schild?], Wiener Zeitung Online</ref>

